WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.560
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.600
Today we are going to have a look at the&nbsp;
incredible capabilities of Midjourney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:16.260
a text to image AI that creates fantasy&nbsp;
images that are so good that it’s frankly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.240
almost unbelievable. It is&nbsp;
a league above any other AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:27.540
I have seen so far. I’ll show you 5&nbsp;
of my favorite examples in a moment.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:34.140
Now, what is this? Text to image means exactly&nbsp;
what it says, we write a short description,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.620
and the AI paints our image. But&nbsp;
things are changing now. We may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:47.040
not even need to be writing our own&nbsp;
prompts. What? Why is that? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:55.200
the GPT-4 AI also just came out, this can be&nbsp;
used with ChatGPT, OpenAI’s amazing assistant.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:03.780
And, one, hold on to your papers, because we&nbsp;
can ask it to break down the key elements of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.940
food photography, what kinds of food should&nbsp;
we use, what should the background look like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:15.780
what about lighting, composition, and so much&nbsp;
more. Photography is an art after all. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:22.740
what did we get here? Did we get some sort of&nbsp;
tutorial, or some ideas? Well, don’t forget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:31.560
this is a chat assistant, so we can ask it to&nbsp;
tabulate all these ideas, and, oh yes! We get a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:38.040
table with detailed instructions for each photo.&nbsp;
These instructions can be dumped into a prompt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:44.280
which ChatGPT will happily do for us, and&nbsp;
then, what do we do with this? Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:51.300
we give this to MidJourney and create these&nbsp;
beautiful hamburgers. Look, these instructions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:58.920
were truly amazing. We can go for a retro-style&nbsp;
top-view, or, if this made us super hungry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:07.920
and we wish to get over the top, we can do this&nbsp;
too. All with the help of two AIs combined. Wow.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.020
The same concept can be applied&nbsp;
to interior design as well. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:18.540
lighting and the mood on this one results&nbsp;
in a stunning picture. I don’t know about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:25.020
you but I still cannot believe that an&nbsp;
AI made this. Or, two AIs if you will.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:31.680
Now, two we can also create not only&nbsp;
images, but videos with these methods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:37.920
Look. If we have made a character that has&nbsp;
the right look, but not quite the right age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:44.280
or we wish to age this character over time, we can&nbsp;
do that too. This video is not to be used as-is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:50.280
so it should not be confused by techniques&nbsp;
that are specifically tailored for that. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.660
if we stop it at individual frames,&nbsp;
these can be used as images.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:03:01.380
Three, it is now able to do something that&nbsp;
none of the previous text to image AIs were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:06.120
able to. Interestingly, none of the previous&nbsp;
previous techniques were unable to synthesize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:13.560
human hands with 5 fingers. Also, they were&nbsp;
often not quite the right shape. And…can that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:20.340
really be? Is it finally solved? Look.&nbsp;
So, let’s see this one. Wow. Now those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:27.120
are not only 5 fingers everywhere, but the&nbsp;
detail and the variety of these images are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:33.720
absolutely incredible. I will now officially&nbsp;
allow it to give a big thumbs up to itself.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:41.580
Four, MidJourney is currently on version 5, and&nbsp;
I found it really surprising that improvement has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:48.660
still not plateaued. For instance, in version&nbsp;
4, it imagined holograms and people to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:56.220
like this, which is not too great. But the same&nbsp;
prompts on version 5. Now that’s what I am talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:02.880
about. And just imagine what version 7 will&nbsp;
be capable of two more versions down the line.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:10.080
But we are not done yet. Not even close!&nbsp;
Five, we have a few more amazing results,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:17.520
and look who this one is coming from. Yes, that’s&nbsp;
right, the legendary computer graphics researcher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.420
Donald Mitchell. Among many other things, he is&nbsp;
the author of the legendary Mitchell-Netravali&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:30.720
filter, which contributes to creating beautiful&nbsp;
high-quality images in light transport simulations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:39.060
and more. He asked for some robot sushi, and&nbsp;
I love how imaginative the results were. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:48.180
works both pass for robots, but they also seem&nbsp;
like edible lunch at the same time. Bravo. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:54.300
what better way to wash it down then asking&nbsp;
for a cocktail from an alien planet. One again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:59.760
they certainly have a strong alien&nbsp;
feel, and I have to say, some of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:06.300
also look drinkable. But, be careful,&nbsp;
who knows what they contain. Loving it.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:12.840
And plus one because I cannot resist. My&nbsp;
favorite. Perhaps everyone’s favorite.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:20.820
Macro photos. Close-up photography of typically&nbsp;
small subjects. I have found this apple pie and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:27.780
this dragon eye, not only the best AI-made&nbsp;
macro images I’ve ever seen, but these are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:33.780
so good they might even rival a journeyman&nbsp;
photographer’s images. What a time to be alive!

